# Multi-tenant source values

Release Desk is sold to many companies. Each tenant has its own workflows, status names, boards, and labels. A literal like `"Done"` is one customer’s word, not a platform rule.

## Do

- Use the source system’s **universal key** when it has one (Jira `statusCategory.key`: `new` | `indeterminate` | `done`).
- Or make the value **configurable** (same pattern as Lifecycle Settings).
- If the indexed field is missing, **do not guess**. Treat it as not classifiable; say a re-sync is needed.

## Do not

- Hardcode a status name, workflow step, or board column as if every tenant uses it.
- Infer “closed” from English words (`Done`, `Closed`, `Resolved`) when a category/key exists.
- Teach the model a `!=` filter the catalog cannot run.

Before writing a status/label/config check: would this break for a tenant who named things differently? If yes, it is not ready.

## Future review (do not “fix” in passing)

Hardcoded name lists still live in: `lib/inbox.ts`, `lib/conversation-context.ts`, `lib/voice/manager-reads.ts`, `lib/dummy-data.ts`, `lib/types.ts`, `lib/utils.ts`, `lib/knowledge-graph.ts`, `lib/enterprise-env-data.ts`, `DbLinkedWorkItems.tsx` (Done/Closed/Resolved → Approved), `summarizeWorkItems` blocked/Pending names, `scripts/jira-ask-benchmark` classifiers.
